# Template for local API keys — copy this file to .env.local and fill in your
# own keys. .env.local is gitignored so real keys never reach the repository.
#
# The prefix is the whole security story here:
#
#   VITE_*     -> compiled into the browser bundle. PUBLIC. Anyone can read it.
#   no prefix  -> stays in the Node/Vite process. Never sent to the browser.
#
# ── MapTiler — public on purpose ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Maps and geocoding run in the browser, so this key has to be reachable from
# client code. That is safe ONLY because MapTiler keys can be locked to a list
# of allowed origins. In https://cloud.maptiler.com/account/keys/ add:
#     http://localhost:5173    (dev server)
#     http://localhost:5174    (Playwright e2e server)
#     https://your-domain.tld  (production)
# Without that list the key works from anyone's site and your quota is theirs.
# A restricted key answers 403 "Key usage restricted" from every other origin.
VITE_MAPTILER_KEY=

# ── Pexels — server-side only ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE THE MISSING VITE_ PREFIX. It is deliberate and load-bearing.
# Pexels offers no origin restriction, so a Pexels key in the bundle is simply
# a published credential. It is therefore only ever read by a server:
#   * dev:        the Vite middleware in vite.config.js reads PEXELS_API_KEY
#   * production: public/api/pexels.php reads a private file OUTSIDE public_html
#                 (see deploy/weathersphere-secrets.example.php)
# The browser only ever calls the same-origin endpoint /api/pexels.php.
# Leave this empty to fall back to the gradient/emoji visuals — nothing breaks.
# Get a free key at https://www.pexels.com/api/
PEXELS_API_KEY=

# ── Google Places — server-side only ────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE THE MISSING VITE_ PREFIX. Same reason as Pexels, plus one: Places API
# (New) authenticates with an X-Goog-Api-Key HEADER, which a browser cannot
# send without publishing the key — and every Places call is billed, so a
# leaked key is someone else's spending on your account.
#   * dev:        the Vite middleware in vite.config.js reads GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY
#   * production: api/places.js (Vercel env var), or public/api/places.php
#                 reading a private file OUTSIDE public_html
# The browser only ever calls the same-origin endpoint /api/places.
# Restrict the key in Google Cloud Console to the Places API (New) only, and
# by server IP address — NOT by HTTP referrer, which does not apply to a
# server-to-server call.
# Leave this empty to skip Google entirely: the photo chain falls straight
# through to Wikimedia and Pexels, and nothing breaks.
# Enable "Places API (New)" at https://console.cloud.google.com/
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=

# ── Mapillary — server-side only ────────────────────────────────────────────
# NOTE THE MISSING VITE_ PREFIX, again. A Mapillary client token
# (MLY|<app id>|<secret>) cannot be origin-restricted, so it must never reach
# the browser.
#   * dev:        the Vite middleware in vite.config.js reads MAPILLARY_ACCESS_TOKEN
#   * production: api/mapillary.js (Vercel env var), or public/api/mapillary.php
#                 reading a private file OUTSIDE public_html
# The browser only ever calls the same-origin endpoint /api/mapillary.
#
# What it is for: geotagged STREET-LEVEL photos — the only coverage available
# for the villages and small towns Google, Wikimedia and Pexels have never
# photographed. Results are always labelled "nearby", never as a photo of the
# place itself.
#
# Licensing: Mapillary imagery is CC BY-SA 4.0. The contributor's username and
# the licence are displayed with every image; an image that cannot be
# attributed is refused rather than shown bare.
#
# KartaView is NOT used by this project. Mapillary is the only street-level
# provider configured — do not add another without reviewing its licence.
#
# Leave this empty to skip Mapillary entirely: the chain falls straight
# through to the Wikimedia text search and Pexels, and nothing breaks.
# Create a token at https://www.mapillary.com/dashboard/developers
MAPILLARY_ACCESS_TOKEN=
